{
 "adaptations": [
  "R-1  `EXPECTED_CLAIMS` rebound from the legacy {block: 133, receipt: 135} to this layout's claim count; `load_inventory` is not called (its only job is that assertion plus index continuity, which this script guarantees by construction).",
  "R-2  `ROWS_TODAY` rebound to {A: a_data_rows, H: h_data_rows - 2, W: 0}: this layout commits its histograms and table helpers as ordinary planes inside the data rows, and its zero-sum row u is the last H data plane, which the tool models as the `h_u` mask pair.  With these values the tool's row arithmetic reproduces A = 306 and H = 290 exactly.",
  "R-3  `tables_from_inventory` rebound to return [] and `with_added` to the identity: the ten legacy range tables with block masks and the twelve added rho_2 sub-row sites do not exist here (one U8 table plus one exp table, each ONE row, each an ordinary claim site with its own reserved pair).",
  "R-4  the SC_ZS slot's H site (the u' pair on the u plane) is not emitted in the tool's view of the claim list, because the tool builds that claim itself (`Builder.add_zsum` with the fresh pair u'). The inventory record keeps it; the derived group counts (A 30 / H 8) include it.",
  "R-5  the H row indices the tool assigns are renumbered onto layout.rs's rows afterwards ([data | u | site pairs | u' | prox] instead of [data | site pairs | u | u' | prox]).  A bijective relabelling: the rank model keys on row NAMES.",
  "R-6  `BILINEAR_SECTIONS` / `WEIGHT_MATMUL_SECTIONS` rebound to this layout's slot names so the score / PV terminals get the two-extension-round coefficient form.",
  "R-7  `run_all` / `run_positive` / `run_negative` / `cross_check_groups` are NOT called: their expectations are hard-coded to the legacy inventory (a W commitment, one 19-member H sum group, an A seam group at index 38, the sm/lm sub-block alternative, 10 histogram tables).  The battery this script runs uses the same imported model functions (Builder / build_model / a_model_groups / h_model_groups / analyze_fast / engines_agree / fa2_groups / identity_check / verdict) with this layout's own expectations.",
  "R-8  sub-row claim sites (the 32-entry T-domain and 64-entry Ht-domain slices: 14 A sites) are presented as single-row claims with a synthetic 8-symbol tail that preserves PCS key equality ((point, c0, len)).  The tool's row model has no sub-row granularity; the true window is recorded in each claim's `sub_row` field.  The approximation is confined to the terminal's column weights, which the with-values models draw at random in any case.",
  "R-9  the two endpoint commitments are modelled separately (one claim, its own pair at rows 2-3, a proximity pair).  The real endpoint geometry has THREE proximity rows (4-6) of seven; modelling two is conservative (fewer mask rows can only disclose more)."
 ],
 "assumptions": [
  "linear model (FA2 sections 13, 15): the verifier's view is the set of group vector entries, proximity entries and terminal values, each a public-coefficient linear form in base-field rows",
  "masks and pads independent and uniform; challenges are seeded stand-ins avoiding the base field (the 2^-64 degeneracies FA2 excludes: e in Fp, lambda = 0, Fp-dependent prox rhos, a row-bit coordinate in Fp)",
  "hashing, Merkle paths, salted leaves, the sampled columns / folded pads and the CFS-masked sumcheck round messages are outside the model (nonlinear); transcript conditioning (a simulator) is outside the model",
  "integer-range side information and cross-proof correlation are outside the model",
  "row bits are taken from the inventory's symbolic points (constants and shared symbols consistent); column tails are per-group stand-ins in the with-values models (n = 4 / 8 columns), which cannot represent the 8-coordinate tails",
  "multi-row histogram slots (256 / 64 / 2 rows) are compressed to 2 rows in the with-values models (FA2's tiny-fixture convention); the per-column models use the real row counts",
  "the two bilinear matmul terminals (score, PV) and, under P3, the QKV / Wo terminals carry the second-extension coefficient form ((1 - e2)(1 - e), (1 - e2) e); it changes no rank (FA3 section 9)",
  "the six private claimed sums (inventory finding 2 / R6) and the CFS slot list (R5) are protocol items outside this linear model; nothing here settles them",
  "numerical rank is not a simulation proof"
 ],
